            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at 13% Gastro Wine",
            "review_text": "Trevor K\n63 contributions\n0\nExcellent selection of wine with average food\nMar 2021\nThis is a proper wine bar with a vast selection of wines to fit everyones budget. It's nicely lit, cozy, and the service was prompt and professional. \n\nI've only been here here once and tried 3 of their small plates. They all sounded great, but could use some work. The beef sliders were on the dry side. The snails were terribly overcooked and the artichoke tasted like fried anything (I would never have guessed it was artichoke). If they were cheaper I probably wouldn't have cared as much, but they're kinda pricey. \n\nI feel like with some fine tuning, this could be a great place for dinner, but for now, I'd only come here to share a bottle of wine.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 24, 2021",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
